{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f876a639",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# HNDL Mock Risk Model \n",
    "\n",
    "**Question:** Which data types are most at risk from \"harvest now, decrypt later\" attacks, and how urgent is migration to post-quantum cryptography?\n",
    "\n",
    "**Core test (Mosca's inequality):** if `X + Y > Z`, the data is already at risk.\n",
    "- **X** = years the data must stay confidential (shelf life)\n",
    "- **Y** = years needed to migrate to post-quantum crypto\n",
    "- **Z** = years until a cryptographically relevant quantum computer exists\n",
    "\n",
    "> Mock project built on public information only. All values below are placeholders to edit and justify, not facts about M&T's actual systems or policies."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d0e51c00",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.width\", 140)\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", 20)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b39a642f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Assumptions\n",
    "\n",
    "Z is uncertain, so use scenarios instead of one number. Cite your sources for the range in the writeup."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cd80503e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "Z_SCENARIOS = {\n",
    "    \"optimistic (Z=10)\": 10,\n",
    "    \"central (Z=15)\": 15,\n",
    "    \"conservative (Z=20)\": 20,\n",
    "}\n",
    "CENTRAL = \"central (Z=15)\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Weights for the risk score (they sum to 1). Change and re-run to test sensitivity.\n",
    "W_INTEREST, W_FEASIBILITY, W_IMPACT = 0.4, 0.3, 0.3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1d6d5e1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Data inventory\n",
    "\n",
    "One row per data type. Scores are 1 to 5. **Every number here is a placeholder: edit it and write a one-line justification in the `note` column.**\n",
    "\n",
    "- `shelf_life_x`: years the data stays harmful if exposed\n",
    "- `migration_y`: years to migrate the systems that protect it\n",
    "- `attacker_interest`: how valuable it is to the adversary\n",
    "- `collection_feasibility`: how easy it is to collect while encrypted\n",
    "- `impact`: harm to customers and the bank if exposed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "39693203",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rows = [\n",
    "    # data_type, category, X, Y, interest, feasibility, impact, note\n",
    "    (\"Customer KYC / PII files\",      \"Personal banking\",   50, 6, 5, 3, 5, \"SSN and DOB never change\"),\n",
    "    (\"Trust and estate documents\",    \"Investments\",        40, 6, 4, 2, 5, \"Lifetime of client plus beneficiaries\"),\n",
    "    (\"Commercial loan files\",         \"Commercial banking\", 10, 5, 4, 3, 4, \"Borrower financials, supplier relationships\"),\n",
    "    (\"Beneficial ownership records\",  \"Commercial banking\", 15, 5, 4, 3, 4, \"Who controls each business\"),\n",
    "    (\"Mortgage servicing records\",    \"Mortgage\",           30, 5, 3, 3, 4, \"Life of loan plus tail\"),\n",
    "    (\"M&A / deal documents\",          \"Commercial banking\",  7, 5, 4, 2, 4, \"Loses value once deal is public\"),\n",
    "    (\"SARs and AML monitoring rules\", \"Internal\",           25, 6, 5, 1, 5, \"Legally restricted; shows detection logic\"),\n",
    "    (\"Long-lived keys / certificates\",\"Internal\",           10, 4, 5, 2, 5, \"Only if they protect archived data\"),\n",
    "    (\"Online banking credentials\",    \"Personal banking\",    3, 3, 3, 4, 3, \"Changes often\"),\n",
    "    (\"Daily payment / wire traffic\",  \"Payments\",            1, 4, 2, 5, 2, \"Loses value within days\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "cols = [\"data_type\", \"category\", \"shelf_life_x\", \"migration_y\",\n",
    "        \"attacker_interest\", \"collection_feasibility\", \"impact\", \"note\"]\n",
    "inv = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=cols)\n",
    "inv"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b41a9c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Mosca margin by scenario\n",
    "\n",
    "Margin = `X + Y - Z`. Positive means the data is at risk (exposure window, in years)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7e0c6acf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for label, z in Z_SCENARIOS.items():\n",
    "    inv[f\"margin | {label}\"] = inv[\"shelf_life_x\"] + inv[\"migration_y\"] - z\n",
    "\n",
    "inv[[\"data_type\"] + [c for c in inv.columns if c.startswith(\"margin\")]]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1a7ae3dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Risk score\n",
    "\n",
    "Mosca tells you *whether* data is exposed. The score ranks *how much it matters*, combining attacker interest, collection feasibility, and impact (0 to 100). Priority = at risk under the central scenario, ranked by score."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b5cd6737",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "inv[\"risk_score\"] = (\n",
    "    (W_INTEREST * inv[\"attacker_interest\"]\n",
    "     + W_FEASIBILITY * inv[\"collection_feasibility\"]\n",
    "     + W_IMPACT * inv[\"impact\"]) / 5 * 100\n",
    ").round(1)\n",
    "\n",
    "central_col = f\"margin | {CENTRAL}\"\n",
    "inv[\"at_risk_central\"] = inv[central_col] > 0\n",
    "inv[\"priority_score\"] = np.where(inv[\"at_risk_central\"], inv[\"risk_score\"], 0)\n",
    "\n",
    "ranked = inv.sort_values([\"priority_score\", central_col], ascending=False)\n",
    "ranked[[\"data_type\", \"shelf_life_x\", \"migration_y\", central_col,\n",
    "        \"at_risk_central\", \"risk_score\"]].reset_index(drop=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a9c7116a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Visualize the margin (central scenario)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d3c8b48c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_df = inv.sort_values(central_col)\n",
    "colors = [\"#C0392B\" if m > 0 else \"#7F8C8D\" for m in plot_df[central_col]]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 5))\n",
    "ax.barh(plot_df[\"data_type\"], plot_df[central_col], color=colors)\n",
    "ax.axvline(0, color=\"black\", linewidth=1)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Mosca margin (X + Y - Z, years). Positive = at risk\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Which data is already exposed to HNDL? (central scenario)\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dfd9fdb0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Sensitivity analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "How does the at-risk list change as the quantum timeline Z moves? A stable ranking across Z values is a stronger finding than any single number."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f69128a8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "z_range = np.arange(5, 36)\n",
    "at_risk_counts = [((inv[\"shelf_life_x\"] + inv[\"migration_y\"]) > z).sum() for z in z_range]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "ax.plot(z_range, at_risk_counts, marker=\"o\", markersize=3)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Years until a cryptographically relevant quantum computer (Z)\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Number of data types at risk\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Sensitivity of HNDL exposure to the quantum timeline\")\n",
    "ax.grid(alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bb6ccb07",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Which data types stay at risk even in the most conservative scenario?\n",
    "conservative_col = f\"margin | {list(Z_SCENARIOS)[-1]}\"\n",
    "inv.loc[inv[conservative_col] > 0, \"data_type\"].tolist()"
   ]
  },
 ],
